Switchboard, November 2026 (against v0.2610.0): bridge channels one at a
time. With dm_only on, upstream drops every channel; the login's metadata
gains a set of chosen channels that pass dm_only's checks, are resynced
next to the DMs on connect, and are seeded once from the channels the login
already bridges. Portals of channels nobody chose are no longer resynced on
connect, so a deselected channel keeps its room and history but gets
nothing new. Resyncs and message fetches read the choice when they run, not
when they were queued, so work queued for a channel does nothing once the
channel is deselected. The helpers and the provisioning endpoints are in
overlay/pkg/connector/switchboard_channels.go; overlay/pkg/slackid keeps the
selection across a relink.

